{
  "_schema": "ether-historical-state-registry-v1.0",
  "_description": "Piecewise-constant geopolitical transition registry. Each interval [t_start, t_end) defines a stable sovereign configuration epoch. Transitions are triggered by historically documented events (treaties, conquests, collapses, revolutions). NO interpolation between intervals is permitted — state is step-constant.",
  "_sources": [
    "Rein Taagepera (1978–1997) — Empire size and duration datasets",
    "CShapes 2.0 (Schvitz et al. 2022) — Post-1886 state territory polygons",
    "Seshat Global History Databank (Turchin et al. 2018) — Polity-level governance metrics",
    "McEvedy & Jones (1978) — Atlas of World Population History",
    "Josiah Cox Russell (1972) — Medieval Regions and their Cities",
    "HYDE 3.4 (Klein Goldewijk et al. 2017) — Land use and population anchors"
  ],
